No. "Shall" is supposed to indicate intent, I believe, while "will" is
supposed to indicate simple future action. "I shall leave for the bus
stop at 3:15, because a bus will be coming by at 3:30." But I think
that in a lot of cases there is little difference between volitional
and non-volitional action--at least in the mind of the speaker--hence
the decline of the use of "shall."
